    public static final String TEXT = new StringBuilder()
            .append("## 0.85.0 (2026-11-24)\012\012* `Remember saved videos` is new in Feed screen, next to the Favorites grid options. As your Favorites load, Hushfeed keeps each video's cover, creator, caption and post date on your phone. When TikTok later marks a saved video as deleted or unplayable, its grey tile shows the kept cover and creator instead, and a tap shows the rest. `Unavailable saved videos` lists them all with a search box. It can only keep what it saw while a video was still up, so tiles that were already grey stay grey (#516).\012* `Fill wide videos too`, right under `Fill the screen with the video`, crops landscape and square videos to cover the screen as well. Fill on its own still leaves those whole, so you see all of a landscape video with bars above and below it. Turn this on and every video fills the screen, showing the middle of a wide one (#505).\012* `Keep your place in chats` stops a chat you've scrolled up in from jumping to the bottom on its own. Coming back from a video you opened in the chat leaves you where you were, and so does sending a reply to an older message. A plain message you send and the down arrow still take you to the newest. It starts off and sits under `Show message times` in Hushfeed settings > Inbox (#503).\012* On the floating bottom bar, `Glass lens on the current tab` is the same thin outline as on TikTok's own bar now, with nothing filled inside, so the video shows through it like it does around it. The glass and see-through bars keep the glass bubble (#483).\012* When the diagnostic report says the phone destroyed TikTok's main screen, it now says why it might have. Either Don't keep activities is on in Developer options, or it gives how full TikTok's memory was, since Android closes an app's screens in the background once three quarters of it is used (#419).\012* `Show how long a LIVE has been on`, with the other LIVE options in Playback, adds how long the host has been live to the small line in LIVE rooms, counted from when the room started and ticking every second. It sits under the room ID when that's on too. A room opened from the LIVE feed shows it once TikTok has that room's start time. It starts off (#494).\012* `Show exact LIVE battle scores` shows a battle's whole score where TikTok caps it for viewers at 1M+ (or at the server's own limit with a + after it) and only the host sees the number. It covers the battle bar, the co-host windows and the high score notice. The supporters list is a page TikTok's server draws, so it isn't covered. It starts off (#495).\012* `Start LIVEs at` is new under `Offer LIVE quality in more rooms`. Pick a quality there and every LIVE room opens at it until you pick another one in a room, and that pick then carries to the next rooms until TikTok closes. A room whose stream doesn't have the quality opens at TikTok's choice. It starts at `The quality you picked last`, which is how rooms opened before (#57).\012* `Skip promo lines` is new under Feed filter, with its own `Promo words` list. When a line of a video's captions has one of your words, like casino or promo code, the video jumps past it and shows Undo, which goes back and lets that part play. It reads the video's own captions, so a video without any plays as usual. It's part of Subtitle tools and starts off (#493).\012* `Show the country and date under the caption` has three settings of its own under Feed screen now: a text size (0 keeps the post date's size, or pick 8 to 48 points), an opacity from 10 to 100, and a shadow under the letters for bright videos (#500).\012* `Tap brings the controls back` is new under `Automatic Clear display`. A tap on a video whose controls it hid shows them again instead of pausing the video, and they hide again after the delay, or after 3 seconds if the delay is shorter (#501).\012* `Burn-in guard dim level` sets how solid the buttons, caption and tabs stay while the burn-in guard has them dimmed, from 0 to 90. It used to be fixed at 25. At 0 they're gone until your next touch (#501).\012* `Hold speed bubble size` is new under `Slide to change the hold speed`. It draws the bubble from 50 to 150 percent of its usual size. Since 0.82.0 the bubble grows with your phone's font size, which made it big with large text on, so set it under 100 to bring it back down (#452).\012* `Fade the controls out` is new under `Automatic Clear display`. The buttons, caption and tabs fade away over a quarter second before the clear instead of vanishing at once, and a touch during the fade brings them back. It starts off (#501).\012* `Date instead of age` is new next to the publish date options. Recent videos show the day they were posted, like 10-12 or Oct 12, where TikTok writes 2d ago, and today's and yesterday's videos get a date too. `Day before month` and `Write the month as a word` change it the same way. It starts off (#461).\012* `SIM spoof`, `Ghost mode`, `Always show publish date` and `Show author region` work on TikTok Lite now. SIM spoof uses the same Region settings as in TikTok. Lite's Ghost mode has `Hide story views`, `Hide profile visits`, `Hide typing` and `Hide online status`. The publish date shows next to the creator's name on every Lite video, For You included, and the date options change it there too. With `Show where a video was posted` on, the country comes after the date, or stands alone where Lite leaves the date off. Lite's video data does carry it, but Lite throws it away while it reads the feed, so Hushfeed picks it up there (#502).\012* `Random time each day` is new under `Keep a streak going`. The message goes out at a different time every day, somewhere between `When to send` and `Latest time`, so friends don't get it at the same minute each day. It starts off (#507).\012* `Jump to a date on Favorites grids` does for your saved videos what the Liked one does for likes. A button in the Favorites grid's top corner starts the list at the year or month you pick, so old saves load without scrolling through thousands of newer ones, and Newest saves goes back. It starts off and sits under `Jump to a date on Liked grids` in Hushfeed settings > Feed screen (#508).\012* `Pick a built-in font` is new under `Import a font file` on the App page. It lists 26 fonts that come with Hushfeed, like Bebas Neue, Lobster, Press Start 2P and VT323, and each name in the list is drawn in its own font. The one you pick becomes your imported font, so turn on `Use an imported font` and restart TikTok to see it (#487).\012* `Delete your picked posts` is new under `Pick videos to save from profile grids` in Downloads. While every post you've picked on a grid is your own, the picking bar gets a trash button. It counts down from 5 with Stop, then deletes the posts from your account one at a time with a short pause between them, and each one leaves the grid as it goes. A deleted post can't be brought back, so it starts off (#487).\012* `Account facts on profiles` shows how many posts an account has. Liked videos, favorites and reposts get a line of their own on the profiles TikTok sends those numbers for, and many profiles come without them. A number TikTok left out or sent as 0 gets no line, since the two look the same (#487).\012* The settings screen now comes in Bulgarian, shown when TikTok runs in Bulgarian or when you pick it under `Hushfeed language`. It's a first pass, so corrections from Bulgarian speakers are welcome (#517).\012* `Export followers and following` can save a JSON or plain text file as well as CSV. Tapping it lists each choice, like `Followers (JSON)` or `Following (Plain text)`. The JSON file has the same details as the CSV, and the plain text one is a username on each line (#487).\012* TikTok Lite's settings no longer list switches that did nothing there. Lite's feed filter works on the videos in the feed and nothing else, so its Feed filter page drops `Hide TikTok Shop in search`, the search tab list, `Show only mutual friends on the Friends tab`, `Latest first on Following`, both offline video switches and `Show how many were filtered`. Its Feed screen page drops `Hide the search bar below videos`, `Hide the playlist bar` and `Hide the event badge`. Every rule that hides a kind of video stays, and so does `Hide inserted cards` (#48).\012* `Swipe LIVEs in your Following row's order` is new with the other LIVE options in Playback. Open a LIVE from the row at the top of Following, and swiping up takes you through the row's other LIVEs in the order they sit there, starting with the next one and then going round to the ones before it. TikTok's own picks come after them, and the row's LIVEs don't show up a second time among those (#511).\012* The Feature Gate Lab leaves TikTok's paid features alone. Gates tied to subscriptions, Super Fan, paid series, LIVE gifts, coins and the like aren't listed any more and can't be saved. A backup or shared profile holding one restores everything else, and a rule saved on one before this stays stored but does nothing.\012* `Remove feed ads` now takes out the sponsored block some searches open with, the \"Ad\" banner for a brand with its videos and a Follow button. Searching \"wildwood\" showed one for a movie (#484).\012* New patch, `Fix notifications on OPPO, OnePlus and realme`. On those phones TikTok also signs up for OPPO's push service, and OPPO only delivers to TikTok as TikTok signed it, so notifications sent that way can't reach a patched TikTok. TikTok now uses Google's push service there, the way it does on a Samsung or a Pixel. Other phones don't change. It's in the default selection, with no switch (#496).\012* With `SIM spoof` on, pictures and thumbnails could stay grey unless a VPN was on. TikTok's network stack picked its image and API servers by the preset's country while the phone was on another country's network. The network stack now gets your real SIM's country and carrier, and the rest of TikTok still sees the preset (#415).\012* With `Keep captions available` on, a video whose caption tracks don't include the one in its original language now shows one of the others. TikTok used to say the video had no captions even though it carried some. The export's Captions line counts those videos as `tracks:unmatched` (#217).\012* `Show the country and date under the caption` no longer sits on the progress bar on videos without a search line under the caption. The line now goes right under the caption and keeps the gap TikTok leaves above the bar. It's white like the name and caption too, not the post time's grey (#498).\012* `Hold TikTok's save button to download` works wherever you press on the save button. TikTok gives some accounts a check that only starts the long press when the press lands right on the icon or its count, and a hold beside them did nothing at all (#499).\012* Record in a LIVE's small window used to do nothing when the room it belonged to had gone away in the meantime. Now it says \"No stream found to record. Reopen the LIVE.\" and writes which part was missing to the log (#413).\012* A translated caption at the top of the comments showed TikTok's raw tags around its hashtags and mentions, like `<h id=\"288\">#flowers</h>`. It shows the plain text now, with the hashtags and mentions where TikTok draws them (#488).\012* Tapping \"more\" on a translated caption at the top of the comments no longer switches it back to the original language. Captions with line breaks kept their original lines for the expanded view (#488).\012* With the floating bottom bar, the top of the pill stuck up over the last row of Home's Community grid. On a page that ends at the bar, like that grid or the other tabs, the strip above the bar now matches the bottom area, so the pill sits inside it. Over videos it still stands a little above the bar (#436).\012* A speed locked on one video and carried to the next ones by `Remember the last speed` now counts as locked there too, so pulling down on those videos lets the lock go. TikTok took them for 1x videos, so the pull just locked the same speed again and the bubble's padlock showed open (#485).\012* With `Hide suggested accounts` on, following someone on a profile you opened from a video no longer leaves an empty \"Suggested accounts\" box under the buttons, and `Keep suggestions on profiles` now shows the suggestions there too. Both only worked on a profile opened on its own page (#462).\012* With `Dark LIVE panels in dark mode` on, a pinned comment's Pinned and timer tags look the same in a LIVE you open from a search result as in any other room. That LIVE plays inside the search's video feed, which never got the room's light colors, so the tags sat on pale pills there (#362).\012* `Hide Balance in the profile menu` no longer leaves a thin empty card where Balance was. Balance sits in a card of its own in that menu, and hiding its only row left the card's edges behind (#194).\012* Photo saves from TikTok's own servers now send the sign-in TikTok's app sends there. Photos from a friend's story were refused without it, every copy, while TikTok showed them fine, and so were photos from private accounts you follow. No other site gets a cookie (#464, #504).\012* Patching takes a lot less memory with most patches selected. All of them together now fit in a 1 GB patcher heap, where they used to run out at 1.5 GB. On a phone where Manager runs 32-bit, every patch now fits with TikTok's bundle and with the APK, where they ran out partway before. Several patches only look through TikTok's code, but every look made the patcher keep an editable copy of the method until the end. And each patch that changes TikTok's resources left the parsed resource table behind for the rest of the run, about 140 MB on the APK (#497, #460, #310, #441, #48).\012* Stickers made from a video get the save box in chats now. Tapping one opens it after TikTok's own preview, and holding one shows Save media, which photo stickers, GIF stickers and AI stickers get in that menu too. TikTok handles all of those apart from its own stickers, so neither showed up for them (#470).\012* With `Hide the music line` on, a video with a music line now has its caption the same distance above the progress bar as a video without one. The music line hid, but the space TikTok keeps under it stayed, so those captions sat a little higher (#512).\012* `Keep captions in Clear display` shows a video's first caption when it's spoken now. 0.84.0 held on to that first caption for the kept line, but on the phone it looked for it in the wrong place and never found it, so the line stayed empty until TikTok sent the next caption, sometimes seconds later (#456).\012* The release tools name only global TikTok's version in the README, the Manager text and the update steps. With TikTok Lite declared too, v0.84.0 went out saying \"TikTok 47.8.2 and 47.9.3\", and the README still pointed at 47.8.3.\012* Three of the patch tree's own checks pass on main again. The SIM spoof's network stack file has its source notice, TikTok Lite's region patch fills its reader stubs from a list the bridge check can read, and the check for made-up TikTok names no longer counts the month pattern `Jump to a date on Favorites grids` formats with.\012\012## 0.84.0 (2026-11-22)\012\012* `Long press` and `Double tap` can now be set to `Save this video`. It saves the video on screen the way the save button does, with your download settings, mini drama episodes included. It's offered when Advanced downloads is patched in (#463).\012* With `Watch LIVEs unseen` on, letting a host see you now lasts for that visit only. Leave the LIVE and you're hidden again the next time you open it. Tap the open eye to stay hidden on your next visit without leaving.\012* Three new LIVE options in Playback change the profile card a tap on a name opens in a LIVE room. `LIVE profile card background` paints the card black, dark gray, light gray or white, and `LIVE profile card text` picks the color of its text, or Automatic for whichever of white and black stands out. Chips, buttons and boxes on the card keep TikTok's colors. `Hide rows on LIVE profile cards` takes off the rows you pick: upcoming LIVE events, products, the shop and its rating, group chat, the bulletin board, the gift gallery and festival honors. They all start off and apply the next time a card opens (#487).\012* `UI scale` is new on the App page. Set its `UI size` below 100 to make TikTok's whole interface smaller, text and buttons alike, so more fits on screen. It takes 50 to 100 and needs a restart, and 100 changes nothing. It works together with `Smaller text sizes`. inxomnyaa sent it in a pull request (#477).\012* `Smaller text sizes` is new on the App page. It adds three stops below the smallest size on TikTok's own Text size slider, in Settings and privacy > Accessibility, so text and everything around it can be smaller than TikTok allows. Pick one there, then restart TikTok. Turning the switch off puts TikTok back on its own smallest size. It starts off. inxomnyaa sent it in a pull request (#476).\012* `Show the room ID and your connection`, with the other LIVE options in Playback, adds a small line to LIVE rooms with the room's ID and how your own connection to the stream is doing. That's ping, latency and download speed, the same numbers TikTok's player keeps for its own LIVE debug panel. A number the player doesn't have for a stream is left out, and nothing about the host's phone is shown. Tap the line to copy the room ID. It starts off (#487).\012* `Account facts on profiles` shows two more lines, the account's gifter level and its SecUID, both from what TikTok already sent with the profile. A detail TikTok left out now says Unknown (TikTok didn't send it) in place of Not sent. Hushfeed shows the username and display name change dates exactly as TikTok sends them, so when an older change has no date, it's TikTok that left it out (#487).\012* `Round the corners on profile grids`, with the other profile grid options under Interface, gives each video on a profile grid 8dp rounded corners. It works on your own profile, anyone else's, the Liked and Favorites tabs, and the videos inside a Favorites collection. It starts off and turns on or off as the grid scrolls, no restart needed (#487).\012* With `More opens the comments` or `Caption above comments` on, the caption at the top of the comments now shows in the language the feed shows it in. If TikTok translates the caption (Always translate, or See translation on that video), the comments get TikTok's own translation, hashtags and mentions included, and See original keeps it as posted. A translation TikTok hasn't fetched yet leaves the caption as posted until the next time you open the comments (#488).\012* `Exit with one Back` is new on the Feed tabs page. One Back on Home leaves TikTok, with no \"Tap again to exit\" toast. From any other tab, Back still goes to Home first, or to the tab `Open TikTok on` picks. It starts off and doesn't need a restart (#489).\012* `Hide the pause icon` is new on the Feed screen page. A tap still pauses and plays the video, but the big play icon doesn't pop up over it anymore. It starts off and doesn't need a restart (#489).\012* `Hide playable games` is new under Feed filter. It takes the mini games tagged Playable out of For You before they show. A creator on your exceptions list keeps theirs. It starts off and needs a restart (#486).\012* `Hide the Tako bubble` also covers the Tako icon some accounts get in the home top bar. inxomnyaa found where TikTok sets it up and sent the hook in a pull request (#475).\012* Two new Comment tools switches for the comment sheet (#479). `Always show the expand button in comments` gives every video's comments the button that stretches them over the whole screen, which TikTok only hands to some accounts. `Keep the video full size under comments` stops the video from shrinking into a small box when the comments open, so they cover its lower part instead. Both start off and take a TikTok restart.\012* `Share any comment`, under Comments, lets you share a comment or send it to a friend when TikTok says it can't be shared. TikTok's server marks those comments, and with the switch on the long-press menu treats them like any other. The link it shares is the video's link with the comment's id on it, the same kind TikTok makes for every comment. It's part of Comment tools and starts off (#481).\012* On TikTok's own bottom bar, `Glass lens on the current tab` is a thin outline now, white on a dark bar and dark on a light one, with nothing filled inside, so it doesn't sit on the icons like a heavy frame. Sliding across the tabs works the same. The glass, floating and see-through bars keep the glass bubble (#483).\012* A name typed after an @ in a bio, like @First Last, opens TikTok's search on the Accounts tab now, where the person is usually the first row. It used to open the Top results. A typed @username still opens that profile, and `Tap @names in bios` turns all of it off (#247).\012* `Identify the song with Shazam` is a new choice for Long press and Double tap, the corners included. It takes 12 seconds from the middle of the video's sound, turns them into a Shazam fingerprint on your phone, and shows the song and artist with Copy and YouTube Music. Only the fingerprint goes to Shazam, never the audio, and only when you use the gesture. The fingerprint code is ported from SongRec.\012* `Unfollow accounts that don't follow you back` is new under Privacy > Clean up your account. It reads who you follow and your followers first, with a running count and Stop, then tells you how many it found and counts down with Cancel before it unfollows them one at a time. An account only counts when your Following list marks it as followed and not mutual and it isn't on your followers list, so the people who follow you back stay followed.\012* `Show what changed since your last visit`, under Profile, puts a line under the @username when you come back to a profile, like \"Since Nov 18: +12 followers, +1 video\". It covers followers, following, likes and videos. When your last visit was earlier the same day, it shows the time instead of the date. The counts stay on your phone, nothing is recorded while the switch is off, and a profile you haven't opened before shows nothing until your next visit. It starts off.\012* `Export followers and following`, under Profile, saves your followers or the accounts you follow as a CSV file in Download/Hushfeed. Each row has the username, name, profile link and IDs, plus whether you follow each other. The list is read at about the pace of scrolling it, with a count and Stop, up to 10,000 accounts. Stop keeps the ones read so far, and the notice says the file is partial.\012* `Save your likes from a TikTok data export`, under Downloads, saves the videos you liked or favorited. Ask TikTok for your data in JSON format (Settings and privacy > Account > Download your data), then pick the file it sends you, or the zip it comes in. Hushfeed tells you how many liked videos and favorites it found and you tick which to save. They save one after another with a count and Cancel, up to 1,000 per run. With `Check for already-saved videos` on, the ones you saved before are skipped, so picking the same file again carries on where the last run stopped. Videos TikTok doesn't have anymore are counted at the end.\012* Ghost mode has a new switch, `Keep likes on this phone`. With it on, a like you give a video turns the heart red but never reaches TikTok, so the creator isn't told and the video stays off your profile's Liked tab. The heart is still red after you reopen TikTok. Unliking one takes it back on the phone. Unliking a video you liked before turning it on still goes to TikTok. `My likes on this phone`, right under it, lists them newest first and opens each video. TikTok's like count doesn't include them, and comment likes still go out.\012* AMOLED dark theme has a new option, `Switch in Hushfeed settings`. It's on unless you turn it off, so your builds stay the same. Off, it leaves out the AMOLED dark mode switch, whose hooks change more of TikTok's code than any other Hushfeed patch, so patching needs less memory, and dark mode stays black. On a computer with every Hushfeed patch picked, the patcher rebuilt 1,777 classes with it off and 2,513 with it on.\012* TikTok Lite 47.8.2 gets its first Hushfeed patches: Settings, Diagnostic tools, Feed filter, Change app name, Trust user certificates, Disable screen capture detection, Network request report, Block contact list access, Block installed app scanning, In-app browser privacy guard and Camera and microphone indicator. Lite has no For You tab to hold, so press and hold the app's icon and pick Open Hushfeed settings. The Feed filter works on For You and leaves a profile's videos and a video you opened alone (#48).\012* `Liquid glass when held` brings the glass lens to your finger now, and it swells more. Move your finger along the bar and the lens goes with it, tab to tab, then slides back to your tab when you let go. The tab under it grows, and on Android 13 and up the tabs bend and split into color at the lens's edge, the way the video does with `Blur the video behind the bar` (#440).\012* With `Keep watching in a small window` on, a LIVE's small window now has previous and next buttons, like a video's. They move to the LIVE above or below the way a swipe does, Record (or TikTok's own button) sits between them, and the one with no LIVE its way shows dimmed (#413).\012* A save that a server turns down now shows up in the diagnostic report's new SAVE REFUSALS section. It names the server, says how it refused (like HTTP 403), and tells whether the save's link had already expired. Before, each refused address only read \"url omitted\" (#464).\012* The diagnostic report's DOWNLOAD PICKER section also lists what's in the video models TikTok keeps beside a video's qualities, each rendition by name and height, so a report can show whether one of them is taller than what Save offers (#471).\012* When TikTok freezes (\"isn't responding\") or crashes in native code, the last exits in the diagnostic report now show the stack Android kept. A freeze lists the main thread's top 40 frames, and a native crash lists its signal and the crashing thread. Android 17's memory limiter and anomaly exits are named too, where the report used to show a bare number.\012* Holding one of TikTok's own stickers in a chat now shows Save media in the menu that opens. It saves the full sticker the same way Save in the sticker box does, and turning off `Save box for chat stickers` takes it away too (#470).\012* `Show the picture before saving`, under `Save a profile picture on a long press`, opens a held profile picture full screen at full size first. Save under it saves the picture, and a tap anywhere else closes it. It starts off (#467).\012* `Report a newer phone to game LIVE` under App tells TikTok's LIVE server you have a Galaxy S25 Ultra while you set up a LIVE. If the server keeps a game LIVE under 1080p 60fps because of your phone, this gives it another chance. It starts off (#459).\012* `Seconds per photo` now goes up to 300, so a photo can stay on screen for up to five minutes in a video made from a photo post (#465).\012* The \"Save photos or a video?\" question has a seconds box now, filled in with `Seconds per photo`. Change it there and that video uses it, and so does the next one, with no trip to settings (#465).\012* Picking photos and videos together in a photo post asks \"Save photos or a video?\" too. Save as video makes one video with each picked video playing in its place between the photos and the post's sound under all of it. Save photos still saves each one as it is (#465).\012* A video made from a post with just one photo runs as long as the post's sound now, up to five minutes, so the music plays to its end instead of stopping when `Seconds per photo` runs out (#469).\012* `Sort pinned videos with the rest` lets a profile's sort put pinned videos in the order with everything else, so Newest first shows them at the date they were posted instead of at the top. It starts off (#466).\012* `Hide or reorder profile tabs` (it used to be `Hide profile tabs`) now has arrows on each tab. Move Liked to the top and it's first on your profile, while the tabs you didn't touch stay where TikTok puts them. `Original order` puts TikTok's back (#466).\012* `Hide Add bio` under App takes the Add bio prompt off your own profile while it has no bio. Edit profile still lets you add one. It starts off (#466).\012* `Hide the people you may know tag` under Feed screen takes that tag away from beside a creator's name. The Friends and Following labels stay (#462).\012* `Hide inserted cards` takes the full-screen people you may know card out of For You too. TikTok doesn't even ask for it while the switch is on, and if one shows up anyway it's dropped from the feed (#478).\012* `Hide stories from accounts you don't follow` clears the recommended stories TikTok mixes into the Inbox's stories tray. Stories from accounts you follow, and your own, stay (#462).\012* `LIVE buttons in the long-press menu` takes Record and Auto tap off the video and puts them in the menu you get by holding the middle of a LIVE. TikTok won't open that menu right after a like, so while Auto tap runs, holding the LIVE stops it instead. Hold again and the menu opens (#359).\012* `Fade the name, date and caption` gives the creator's name, the date, the caption and the music line their own opacity over the video (#462).\012* `Write the month as a word` shows TikTok's date by the creator's name as Oct 12, or 12 Oct with `Day before month` on (#461).\012* `Use an imported emoji font` draws emoji in a font file you pick, separately from the text font. It's part of `Use system font` and needs Android 12 or newer (#458).\012* `Video bitrate limit` keeps a heavy video from eating your data. Anything over the limit plays a lighter version, and videos under it aren't touched (#454).\012* Double tap and Long press can mark the video on screen as not interested, with the same follow-up choices as the button. It needs the Not interested patch (#452).\012* The diagnostic report says when TikTok's main screen starts over while the app is still runnin")
            .append("g, and what happened to the screen before it. That's what a feed jumping back to the top with no crash looks like (#419).\012* With `Stop recording watch history` in the patch set, the diagnostic report counts TikTok's view reports, the ones Watch history is built from. It shows how many were made and how many TikTok groups into one send. Then it counts the ones sent on their own, sent together, dropped because TikTok's server told the app to slow down, held back by `Keep videos out of Watch history` or failed, with the last failure's reason (#448).\012* The diagnostic report's IMAGE LOADS section counts failed images by how they failed, not one line per picture, so a few hundred refusals from one server read as one line with a count. Request headers in a failure show their names only, never their values. The section also says which country TikTok has placed your phone in and how it decided, next to the SIM country Hushfeed is showing it, so a report can tell when the two don't match (#415).\012* `Freeze TikTok's experiments` under App keeps the settings TikTok's servers already sent and ignores new ones, so a layout or feature TikTok starts testing on your account doesn't show up out of nowhere. If something in TikTok stops working, turn it off so the fix can reach you. It starts off. The switch has been in the patches since 0.81.0 without a note here.\012* Hushfeed moves to TikTok 47.9.3, and only that one. 47.8.3 isn't supported anymore. Get the 47.9.3 bundle or APK from APKMirror and patch it with your usual signing key.\012* With `Copy the link with one press on Share` on, the Share button's screen reader label says it copies the link as soon as a video shows. Before, it kept TikTok's usual Share label until you'd pressed the button once.\012* Searching for a product no longer logs an error, or shows an error toast with diagnostic logging on, when TikTok or the videos themselves mark every result on a page as an advert. The page still shows as TikTok sent it, and the diagnostic report says why. A page where every card carries an advert's shape still counts as an error, since that points at a broken check.\012* On a tablet held sideways, opening a profile from search or a picture in the comments no longer flips the screen to portrait. The new `Turn profiles and comment pictures on tablets` patch has both turn with the rest of TikTok wherever TikTok's own check lets its main screen turn. Phones aren't affected (#490).\012* With `Translate button in comments` on, the suggested search at the top of the comments stops before the translate button instead of running under it (#479).\012* `Translate button in comments` now offers the restart button when you flip it. TikTok keeps one comment sheet for the whole feed and only checks for the button when it builds that sheet, so the change waited for a restart anyway.\012* `Remove feed ads` takes another kind of search ad out of the results. Some search ads carry their video tucked inside the card rather than on it, and TikTok itself doesn't call them ads when asked, so they stayed in the grid (#484).\012* With `Floating bottom bar` and `Hide the bottom tab names` on, the bar lines each tab up by its icon, and an empty box inside a tab doesn't count as the icon anymore. TikTok's Create tab can carry one, and lining up by it could leave the + sitting higher than the other icons (#474).\012* TikTok doesn't freeze and crash anymore with thousands of offline videos saved. Every few minutes TikTok checked how many saved videos were still unwatched by loading all of them, and with a big `Custom offline videos limit` that filled its memory. It asks the database for the number now (#482).\012* With `Slide to change the hold speed` on, pulling down to lock keeps the speed the bubble shows on every video. Once a lock carried its speed into the next videos, TikTok counted each of them as locked already, so a slide and a pull there unlocked the video and dropped it to 1x instead. A pull without sliding still unlocks (#485).\012* `My watch history` is up to date when you come back to it from a video you opened in it. It used to show the list from before you left until you closed and reopened it.\012* The checklist under `Hide Settings and privacy rows` now names the rows the way TikTok 47.9.3 shows them, in the same order as the page, and it has the Visibility and Interactions rows too, like Blocked accounts, Mentions and Direct messages. Before, those showed up under made-up names like \"Shared links\", and a few others still had their old labels, like Inbox mode for what's now Inbox & Messaging. In German, Italian, Russian and five more languages, Family Pairing now has TikTok's current name too (#244).\012* With `Bottom bar height` on anything but TikTok default, the tab icons no longer sit on top of their names. TikTok pads its tabs differently once the bar's room isn't the size it expects, and the new height counted as unexpected, so the icon and the name got pushed into each other. On a taller bar they keep the same gap as on TikTok's own bar now. On a shorter one they shrink a little with the bar, so the selected tab's outline still fits around them.\012* With `Bottom bar height` on Tall or Taller, the search strip at the bottom of a video no longer slides under the bar, and on Short or Shorter it no longer floats above the bar with a gap. The caption, the strip and its progress line keep TikTok's distance from the bar at every height now.\012* TikTok no longer crashes a few seconds after launch on some phones with \"Final field cannot be written to\". The Feed filter's check on videos TikTok saved for later wrote a value TikTok had marked read-only (#472).\012* With `Log diagnostics` on, Hushfeed settings no longer log a failure for the App icon row each time the page opens or refreshes. It stays out of the diagnostic report, and `Show failures on screen` doesn't pop an error for it anymore. That row saves nothing, so it was never a missing setting.\012* `Copy quick report` puts the report together in the background, so the settings page no longer stalls while it reads saved crashes. The other patch bundles line is filled in on the first copy too, where it used to ask you to copy again.\012* Native crash lines in the diagnostic report keep their function names. A name like `HttpNetworkSession::GetSocketPool` read as a session value and was blanked.\012* The Feature gate lab's list of TikTok settings is right where TikTok's code branches. A few entries were named after a setting loaded on another path, or showed another setting's default, and some settings read after a jump weren't listed at all.\012* `Show account country` and `Block this commenter` show up when you hold a comment on accounts where TikTok is trying out its newer share-style comment menu. That menu never got the rows. With either switch on, TikTok opens its regular menu instead, and the share button on comments stays (#417).\012* With `Keep the middle unstretched` on, search results play in the app's window like the feed does. A search video on a layer of its own used to leave every video cropped and stretched until the next restart (#468).\012* With `Keep the middle unstretched` on, a video's cover picture keeps the same size as its video. When TikTok played a video on a layer of its own, the cover could still take the whole screen, so it showed at the wrong size and flickered as the video replaced it. Once that happens the video and its cover are both cropped and stretched evenly, and the diagnostic report says so (#468).\012* Searching the settings for `SIM country preset`, or just \"preset\", finds that row now. It used to find nothing.\012* With `Auto-advance videos` and `Keep playing in the background` both on, a creator's videos keep coming after you start one from their profile and leave the app. TikTok used to play that first video and stop. `Auto-advance session limit` counts these too, and screen-time holds stop them the same way (D292).\012* A copy made with Morphe's `Clone app` can log in with the default selection now. `Run beside the store app` is part of Simple mode, and it does nothing on a copy that keeps TikTok's own package name. Without it, TikTok's servers wouldn't give the renamed copy a device ID, so every login said you'd hit the maximum number of attempts (#455, #284).\012* The date and length on profile grids don't get cut in half anymore. The label's bar now grows when it needs a third line (#449, #462).\012* Patching no longer stops at `Settings` when TikTok's Open Debug row can't be found. You lose only the Hushfeed row in TikTok's settings, and holding Home still opens the page (#460).\012* `Save episodes` loads a mini drama's episode list again. It used to stop at \"Couldn't load the episodes\" (#463).\012* The `Save episodes` list goes past the free episodes of a drama you haven't unlocked, and saving one of those gets the whole episode. TikTok's list sends those episodes without their video, so Hushfeed asks for each one on its own instead of stopping at \"This video isn't available as a complete file\" (#463).\012* When TikTok's server turns down every copy of an original photo, `Download original photos` saves the copy TikTok shows on screen instead of stopping at \"None of the photos could be saved\" (#464).\012* With `Hide suggested accounts` on, following someone doesn't leave an empty Suggested accounts box on their profile anymore. Turn on `Keep suggestions on profiles` if you'd rather keep that row while the other suggestions stay hidden (#462).\012* `Play original audio` also covers videos TikTok dubs with a whole second copy of the video, which is how some mini dramas get theirs. Saving one of those with the switch on keeps the original sound too (#463, #444).\012* The note on the `White on black`, `Black on white` and `Material You` app icons, and on themed icons, has clean round edges now. TikTok's own note has dents that its colored echoes normally cover.\012* `Keep captions in Clear display` shows a video's first caption right away, sits near TikTok's own caption spot when it hasn't seen one yet, and stays above the progress bar (#456).\012* The country and date line doesn't get cut off anymore when you open a long caption, and the caption above it keeps every line after you open or close it with more and less (#457).\012* `Show the country and date under the caption` keeps the two together on photo posts and on videos with no caption. With no caption they go right under the creator's name (#453).\012* A sorted profile grid loads up to 1,000 videos on its own before it sorts, up from 300, so a long profile's oldest and longest videos make it into the order. On a long profile that takes around 35 seconds. Tap the loading grid to see the order it has right away, and your scrolling loads the rest. A slow connection stops after 45 seconds the same way. The notes under the profile and sound page sort settings say 1,000 now too, where they still said 300 (#180).\012* With `Dark LIVE panels in dark mode` on, the Unmute and Remove buttons in a LIVE's Muted and Blocked lists show their label in white. The buttons are a see-through gray on the dark sheet and the label stayed dark gray on them, so you could barely read it (#362).\012* With `Dark LIVE panels in dark mode` on, every row of a LIVE's Muted, Blocked and Moderation lists stays readable as you scroll. Rows the list brought in while scrolling kept their dark gray text on the dark sheet, and the readable ones seemed to jump around as the list reused them (#362).\012* With `Dark LIVE panels in dark mode` on, an outlined button on a LIVE settings page gets a white outline with its label inside it. The white filled the whole button, so the Moderation list's buttons showed up as blank white boxes (#362).\012* With `Dark LIVE panels in dark mode` on, the \"Find an open guest spot\" bar under a LIVE guest's card reads light on a dark gray bar. TikTok always draws that bar in its light colors, so its text and arrow were black on the black sheet (#362).\012* With `Dark LIVE panels in dark mode` on, a pinned comment's Pinned and timer tags sit right on the video again, the way they look with the switch off. They still had pale see-through pills behind them, because the comment's rows took the colors meant for the dark panels (#362).\012* The Settings patch marks itself applied in one place for TikTok and TikTok Lite, after the last of its changes went in. Lite's half used to do it on its own, which broke the check that every patch does that last, and that check had failed since Lite support came in.\012* The GitHub release notes leave out the Build changes and the What was checked list now. Build changes are still listed here in the changelog.\012* The build runs on Gradle 9.9.1, which fixes the three Gradle security advisories published on November 10. The wrapper jar and the distribution checksum come from services.gradle.org.\012* The patches are built with Morphe patcher 2.5.0, the one stable Morphe Manager 2.7.0 and morphe-desktop 2.3.0 ship. Bundles from now on need Manager 2.7.0 or newer, and the README and the bug form say so.\012* Patching for a phone, the full patch check and the release tools work again now that some patches also name TikTok Lite. They read TikTok as the target because every patch names it, and Lite's versions no longer count. Before this they stopped with \"Expected one compatible package\".\012* The register check that runs after patching accepts the 47.9.3 APK. It still expected 47.9.2's checksum, and moving to a new TikTok build now swaps that checksum along with the version.\012* The scripts that move the patches to a new TikTok build are in `scripts/retarget/` now. `retarget.ps1` takes the old and new fixture folders and runs the whole renaming pass, and concepts/patch-development.md says how to read what it reports.\012* `Custom offline videos limit` stops the patch with an error if TikTok ever puts a branch between its clean-up answer and the return the patch rewrites. The check for that never matched an if or a goto before.\012* The README's advice for a 32-bit Manager now says to patch the bundle and leave out the patches you don't need. It used to say every patch fits once AMOLED dark theme's `Switch in Hushfeed settings` is off, which came from 1 GB tests on a computer. On a phone running a 32-bit Manager 2.7.0 (1.5 GB for the patcher), TikTok 47.9.3's APK ran out of memory about halfway through every patch with that option on or off.\012\012## 0.83.0 (2026-11-17)\012\012* Hushfeed moves to TikTok 47.8.3, and only that one. 47.7.3 isn't supported anymore. Get the 47.8.3 bundle or APK from APKMirror and patch it with your usual signing key so your login and settings come along.\012* You can switch the home screen icon from Hushfeed's settings now, without patching again (Discussion #114). Turn on `Pick the icon in Hushfeed` in the Custom launcher icon patch and an `App icon` row shows up under Appearance with every icon style, plus Your icon if you set a picture or a background color. Needs Android 8 or newer. Some home screens drop the icon when it changes, so if yours does, add TikTok back from the app list.\012* `Liquid glass when held` makes the glass lens on the main feed's tabs react to your finger, the way the iPhone's tab bar does. Hold a finger on the tabs and the lens swells, then it wobbles back when you let go. With `Blur the video behind the bar` on Android 13 and up, the video under the lens bends harder while you hold it and splits into a little color at its edge. It works with or without `Slide across the tabs` and sits under `Glass lens on the current tab`.\012* `Tap a video to remove it` (under Clean up your account on the Privacy page) turns a tap in your own Liked videos, Favorites or Reposts into a removal. The video dims while TikTok takes it back, then leaves the grid, and nothing opens. Other people's profiles and your own videos open as usual. It's off by default. (#401)\012* `Remove all comments` and `Remove selected comments` are new on the Privacy page, under Clean up your account (#442). The first deletes every comment you've posted, one at a time with a short pause between them, and shows a count with Stop while it goes. The second opens your comment history so you can tick just the ones you want gone. Either way you get a few seconds with Cancel before anything is deleted.\012* `Play original audio` plays mini dramas and other videos in their own language instead of the AI dub TikTok picks for your app language (#443). Captions and translations stay as they are, so you can keep TikTok in your language. Turn it on in Hushfeed settings > Playback. It's off by default.\012* `Swipe left` has a new choice, `Save to a collection` (#445). A left swipe on a video opens TikTok's own popup for saving it to one of your collections, the same one you get by holding the Favorites button, so you never land on the creator's profile by accident. It works in Clear display too, where the buttons are hidden. Pick it under Hushfeed settings > Feed screen.\012* `Group likes per comment` gives each comment or video people liked one row in the Inbox's Likes list, with everyone who liked it counted. TikTok's server only bundles the likes that come in close together, so a comment that keeps getting likes used to fill the list with rows like \"A likes your comment\" and \"B, C and 5 others like your comment\". Each row now sits where its newest like is, and older pages fold into it as you scroll. It starts off, sits under `Expand activity list` in Hushfeed settings > Inbox and applies the next time the Likes list loads. Thanks to @X-15 (#446).\012* `Split activity list` turns the Inbox's Activity page into two of TikTok's own lists, your newest comments and replies on top and likes below, each scrolling and loading on its own, with the same Like and Reply buttons on each comment. TikTok mixes both into one list and puts likes it ranks as priority in front, so a reply to you could sit below twenty likes. The bar between the two lists stays put. Its ⇅ swaps which list is on top, its ✕ hides whichever list is below until the `Show` bar at the bottom brings it back, and Hushfeed remembers both. The Activity menu still works. Pick Likes, Comments or Mentions to see just that list, and Activity to get the split back. With `Search loaded activity` on, each list gets its own search bar. It starts off, sits under `Expand activity list` in Hushfeed settings > Inbox and applies the next time the page opens. Thanks to @X-15 (#447).\012* Picked photo posts can come out as one video. With `Save photo posts as a video` on, pick two or more photo posts on a grid and tap Save, and you're asked whether you want one video or one per post. One video plays each post's photos in the order you picked them, each with its own sound, and any videos you picked still save on their own (#430).\012* `Offer full screen in more LIVEs` gives LIVEs streamed from a phone the full screen button TikTok keeps for LIVEs from a computer or a shared screen. TikTok still shows it only when the stream is wide, and a tap turns the room sideways to fill the screen (#57).\012* `LIVE name alerts` tells you when your name comes up in a LIVE. It catches chat lines that mention you or type your name, and in a room with captions on, your name said out loud. With TikTok's notifications on you get a notification that vibrates, and with them off a banner shows in the room. Your handle and TikTok name are always listened for, and `Names to listen for` adds the other names people call you. On Android 13 and newer, `Listen for your name` also listens to the LIVE's sound through your phone's own speech recognition, so a name said out loud counts in rooms without captions too. In a LIVE you're watching unseen, that listening starts once you tap the eye. They all sit under `Auto tap speed` in Hushfeed settings > Playback, with `LIVE controls` patched (#424).\012* `Watch LIVEs unseen` keeps you off the viewer list of the LIVEs you open, so the host doesn't see you come in. The LIVE stays open and keeps playing while you're hidden, and doesn't skip ahead to the next one. A crossed-out eye in the room means you're hidden, and a tap on it lets that host see you until you close TikTok. It starts off and sits under Ghost mode in Hushfeed settings > Privacy (#420).\012* Diagnostic reports get an `IMAGE LOADS` section. It counts the images TikTok fetched from each server since it started, how many of them failed and why, so a report can show what's behind covers and avatars that stay gray. Only the server's name goes in, never the image's address (#415).\012* `Crop and stretch to fill the screen` covers the whole screen with a bit of both. It crops half as much as `Fill the screen with the video` and stretches half as much as `Stretch the video to the screen`, so neither one stands out. Turn it on in Hushfeed settings > Playback (#421).\012* `Keep the middle unstretched` covers the whole screen and leaves the middle of the video at its own shape, so faces in the middle look normal. A little comes off each side, and the rest of the gap is made up along the top and bottom, stretched least where they meet the middle. It needs Android 13 or newer and asks for a restart, and until TikTok restarts it crops and stretches like `Crop and stretch to fill the screen` (#421).\012* `Caption spot in Clear display` lets the caption you keep in Clear display sit lower, near the bottom, instead of up where TikTok puts it to clear the description. Clear display hides the description anyway, so the line doesn't have to float over an empty gap. `Caption height in Clear display` lifts it from whichever spot you pick. It's under `Keep captions in Clear display` in Hushfeed settings > Interface (#428).\012* `Share the video after a save` opens Android's share sheet with the file as soon as a video is saved, video stories included, so you can send it straight to WhatsApp, Telegram or any other app without digging through your gallery. Photo posts you save as a video count too. Picked videos saved together still get the usual notice. It starts off and sits under `Show download progress` in Hushfeed settings > Downloads (#423).\012* `Long-press Profile for Activity center` opens TikTok's Activity center when you hold the Profile tab, so your watch history, comments and time spent are one press away. A tap on Profile works as before, and while `Long-press Profile for Watch history` is on, that one keeps the press. If TikTok hasn't given your account an Activity center, the press opens Settings and privacy instead (#425).\012* `Look up a commenter's country` adds Show account country to the menu you get by holding a comment. Tap it and you'll see where TikTok says that account is based. TikTok keeps that to itself for most accounts now, so you'll usually get the country its latest videos were posted from instead. The answer pops up at the bottom, and with `Show where commenters are from` on, that account's comments show it from then on. `Account country on profiles` puts the same lookup on a profile's share sheet as an Account country button. Both start off (#417, #201).\012* `Hide the summary on LIVE previews` takes away the AI Summary card TikTok puts at the bottom of a LIVE in the feed, the one that sums up what the stream is about. Some LIVEs get a newer style of that card, and the switch hides that one too. It starts off and sits under `Hide the Service+ row under LIVE previews` in Hushfeed settings > Playback, with `LIVE controls` patched. Pausing Hushfeed shows the card again (#418).\012* `Stretch the video to the screen` is a third choice under Playback, next to Fit and Fill. It covers the whole screen without cropping anything by making the video a little taller or wider. Videos far from your screen's shape stay as they are, so a landscape video never gets squashed into a tall one. It starts off, and turning it on turns the other two off (#406).\012* `Hide Settings and privacy rows` takes TikTok's own rows you never use off its Settings and privacy page, like Ads or Shake to report. Tick them in the checklist under `Hide the Hushfeed row` in Hushfeed settings > App and they're gone the next time that page opens. A section that loses every row loses its title too, and pausing Hushfeed brings them all back (#244).\012* `Show message times` puts the time each message was sent under it in a chat, in small gray text below the bubble. TikTok only shows a time above a message that comes after a gap. It starts off and sits under `Turn off swipe to reply` in Hushfeed settings > Inbox.\012* `Glass Stories button on Following` swaps the flat gray Stories button at the top of the Following feed for glass with round ends, and on Android 12 and up the video behind it shows through blurred. It starts off and sits under `Hide the LIVE row on Following` in Hushfeed settings > Feed screen. Turning it off or pausing Hushfeed brings TikTok's own button back (#409).\012* `Hide search result tabs` takes tabs you never use off the strip above search results. Tick Shop, LIVE, Places or any other tab TikTok shows you and it's gone from every search, while Top always stays. The checklist sits under `Hide TikTok Shop in search` in Hushfeed settings > Feed filter, and it shows each tab by name in your settings language.\012* `Delete watched offline videos` clears the offline videos you've already watched every time TikTok starts, so the next download fills their spots with new ones. A video counts as watched once it's been on screen. It starts off, sits with the offline rows in Hushfeed settings > Downloads, and shows how many unwatched videos you have left.\012* `Bottom bar height` makes TikTok's bottom bar shorter or taller, in five steps from Shorter to Taller. Videos and the other tabs make room for it at the new height. It sits under `Bottom bar icons` in Hushfeed settings > Feed tabs and takes hold after a restart.\012* `Hide profile tabs` takes tabs off the strip above a profile's videos. Tick Videos, Reposts, Liked videos, Favorites, AI theater, Shop or any of the others and they're gone from every profile you open, yours included, so you can keep just Favorites and Liked if that's all you swipe between. With Videos hidden a profile opens on the first tab left, and at least one tab always stays. The checklist sits under `Hide profile shortcuts` in Hushfeed settings > App and takes hold after a restart (#392, #399).\012* `Fix Spotify login` gets Add to Spotify past its sign-in. The Spotify app won't link a patched TikTok, so you now sign in on Spotify's own page inside TikTok and it links your account from there. It's on as soon as you patch it in, with no switch.\012* The settings screen now comes in Arabic, shown when TikTok runs in Arabic. It's a first pass, so corrections from Arabic speakers are welcome (D307).\012* `Video download codec` picks which codec a saved video comes in when TikTok has the same quality in both. Automatic keeps H.264, which nearly every player opens. HEVC first saves the HEVC copy, which is often sharper since TikTok can send its H.264 at a lower bitrate. H.264 only never saves HEVC, for older players and TVs. It sits under `Video download quality`. Thanks to @Tegar30 (#400).\012* `Pick which stories to save` lets you save more than one of someone's stories at once. With it on, saving a story opens a checklist of their stories with the one you're watching already ticked, and a story you held to save waits, paused, until the list closes. Tick the others you want, or Pick all, and they save together with one progress count. TikTok loads a person's stories a few at a time as you watch, so the list says how many are still to come. It starts off and sits under `Save a story from its share sheet` in Hushfeed settings > Downloads (#393).\012* `Check for already-saved videos` now covers the photo posts TikTok saves by itself too, on Android 10 and newer. That's live photos, plus still photos while `Download original photos` and `Save photo posts as a video` are both off. Save one twice and you get Open or Save again first, and the post gets its ✓ on profile grids like the rest (#197).\012* `See-through status bar` now also works on videos you open from search, a profile or your Liked and Favorites. A new `Shade behind the status bar` puts a soft dark fade behind the clock and icons so they're still easy to read over a bright video. It's off to start with and sits right under `See-through status bar` (#407).\012* `See-through bottom bar` runs the video all the way down under the gesture bar now. The feed used to stop just above it, so on phones with gesture navigation the handle sat on a black strip. The tabs, the caption and the buttons stay where they were. With `Fill the screen with the video` on, a video opened from search, a profile or your Liked videos goes under the gesture bar too, and its comment bar stays put (#408).\012* `Export comments` now loads every reply under the comments first, so you don't have to open each thread by hand anymore. While it works, the count beside the buttons shows how many replies have come in and the button you tapped turns into Stop. Stopping, or closing the comments, saves what's loaded so far. The message after the export says when some replies didn't load, and a JSON file marks it with `replies_complete`. It stops at 3,000 replies. Every reply now sits right under its comment in the file, even ones you opened after scrolling further down, and if you leave TikTok while replies load, the save screen opens when you come back.\012* Favorites grids get their own order. `Sort loaded videos on Favorites grids` starts at `Same as profile grids`, and the sort button on a Favorites grid now changes only that order, so Liked and your profile keep theirs. It sits right under the Liked row (#180).\012* Collections you make inside Favorites can be sorted too. `Sort loaded videos in collections` starts at `Same as Favorites grids`, has the same orders, and a collection gets the sort button in its corner, which changes only the collection order. Open a video from a sorted collection and swiping up follows that order. A video pinned on its cr")
            .append("eator's profile sorts in with the rest there, and the collection's own top rows stay where they are (#180).\012* `Show the country and date under the caption`, next to `Show the country as a flag`, puts the creator's country and the post date on a line of their own right below the caption, so the row with the name stays short. The line uses the same small print as the date, exact times and the saved mark included. Photo posts get the line too, and a post with no caption keeps both in the row. Turn it off and both go back where they were (#410).\012* `Glass lens on the current tab` works on any bottom bar now, the glass one and every other style. Turn it on with whatever bar style you use, TikTok's own included, and the bubble sits behind your tab. `Slide across the tabs` and `Haptics on the tabs` come along with it. On a white bar the lens turns a soft gray so you can still see it, and TikTok's own bar color stays underneath (#416).\012* The small window from `Keep watching in a small window` has previous and next buttons on both sides of play and pause, so you can move through the feed without opening TikTok. An arrow dims when there's no video that way. A tall video's window is too narrow for three buttons, so it shows play and next until you make it bigger. Leave a LIVE with the switch on and it keeps playing in TikTok's own small window, which TikTok hardly ever offered before. It works on tablets and foldables too, and on phones TikTok has mistaken for a tablet, which it used to leave out. When `Record LIVEs you watch` is on, that window gets a Record button next to its play and pause. Tap it again to stop, and the recording saves like one started from the room (#413).\012* Feature Gate Lab has a `Visual search on paused videos` preset from Japan's builds. It turns on the search tag TikTok puts on things in a paused video, which opens its visual search. Like the other presets it needs the Lab's overrides switch and a TikTok restart, and TikTok's server still decides which videos get a tag (#98).\012* `Day before month` writes the date by the creator's name day first, so 09-29 reads 29.09 and an older video's 2024-03-07 reads 07.03.24. Ages like 2d ago stay as they are. With `Show the time to the second` on, that date goes day first too, like 29.09.26 with `Short date` or 29 Sep 2026 without. It starts off and sits under `Short date` in Hushfeed settings > Interface (#438).\012* Hushfeed's buttons on videos can be smaller or bigger now. `Size of the buttons on videos` goes from Smallest to Large, and `Line them up over the right column` stacks them above TikTok's own buttons on the right, starting over the avatar, so they move with that column instead of staying where you dragged them. Both sit right under the buttons in Hushfeed settings > Interface. `Hold TikTok's save button to download` makes a press and hold on TikTok's own save button save the video with your download settings, while a tap still adds it to Favorites. It sits under `Hold speed on Favorites` and needs `Long-press controls` and `Advanced downloads` patched (#433).\012* `Settings theme` keeps Hushfeed's own settings and pop-ups dark or light whatever mode TikTok is in. `Match TikTok` is the old way and stays the default, while `Always dark` and `Always light` hold that look. The row is on the first page of Hushfeed settings, under `Pause Hushfeed`, and the page repaints as soon as you pick (#434).\012* `Size of the LIVE buttons` makes Hushfeed's Record, Auto tap, Block and eye buttons in a LIVE room smaller, so they stop covering the room's own buttons on a small screen. Pick Small or Smallest in Hushfeed settings > Playback, under `Auto tap speed`. Normal keeps the size they've always had (#359).\012* `Hushfeed language` shows Hushfeed's settings and messages in the language you pick, even when TikTok and your phone are set to another one. Each language is listed in its own name, and `Match TikTok` keeps the old way and stays the default. It's on the first page of Hushfeed settings, under `Settings theme` (#431).\012* `Fill a tall screen instead`, right under `Fit the video to the screen`, gives a folding phone both looks. The tall front screen gets cropped to fill like `Fill the screen with the video`, while the big screen opened up (or a phone turned sideways) keeps the whole video. It switches as you fold and unfold (#345).\012* `Save episodes button in the share sheet` puts Save episodes in the share sheet of a mini drama episode (#444). Tap it and you get that drama's episodes as a list, with the one you're watching already checked, so you can pick the ones you want and save them in one go. An episode you haven't unlocked only saves the short preview TikTok sends, and its row says so. Turn it on in Hushfeed settings > Downloads.\012* `Hide LIVEs from accounts you don't follow` clears the LIVE circles TikTok mixes into the Inbox's stories tray from people you don't follow. LIVEs from accounts you follow stay put. `Hide the Widget circle` drops the circle at the end of the tray that pitches TikTok's home screen widget, and the widget itself keeps working. Both start off and sit under `Hide On this day` in Hushfeed settings > Inbox (#449).\012* `Hide view counts on profile grids` takes the view count and its little play icon off every video on a profile grid. If you've turned on dates, lengths or the engagement rate for grids, they move up into that spot. It starts off and sits under `Show video length on profile grids` in Hushfeed settings > Feed screen (#449).\012* TikTok no longer closes when it asks your screen for a slower refresh rate. `Keep the screen's refresh rate` had caught its own change of the rate along with TikTok's, so the first time TikTok asked, Hushfeed kept handing the request back to itself until TikTok crashed, with the switch on or off. TikTok doesn't ask on every phone, which is how it went unnoticed.\012* On TikTok 47, switches that work by changing one of TikTok's own settings reach the copy TikTok reads again. TikTok 47 keeps those settings twice and reads almost all of them from the second copy, which Hushfeed didn't look at. That covers `Keep the Favorites tab`, `Use non-personalized search`, `Show the progress bar thumbnail` and `Stop the blink under the bar`, and lets `Keep the middle unstretched` work there. Feature Gate Lab rules on those settings take hold too (#448).\012* `Hide surveys` catches the Not interested and Interested buttons under a video's description again when TikTok draws them from one of its templates, which got past both of the old checks. The diagnostic report also names what type each feed component was (#439).\012* With `Open the comments at full height` on, TikTok's faded search icon no longer sits on top of the X that closes the comments. That icon belongs over the small video TikTok shows above the comments, and at full height there's no video up there for it (#435).\012* The Advanced downloads description sent you to Downloads for `Show the save button on videos`, but the switch is in Feed screen under Buttons on videos. The description says where it is now, and Downloads has a row that takes you straight to it. Searching settings for \"download button\" finds it too (#299).\012* The \"Saving video\" message doesn't sit on top of the saved banner anymore. It still did when another message was waiting behind it, like the sound's with `Save the sound as well` on. Where the sound went, and the notes about a watermarked copy or a possible second copy, are lines on the banner now (#299).\012* With `Stretch the video to the screen` on, the still picture TikTok shows before a video starts gets stretched the same way as the video. It used to show a different shape and flick when the video took over (#421).\012* With Ghost mode on, stories you watched stay watched after you close and reopen TikTok, in the inbox and on profiles. TikTok never heard you watched them, so their rings used to light up again once TikTok forgot the play (#427).\012* `Show where a video was posted` no longer shows FAKE-AD on ads. TikTok gives ads a made up country, so only a real two-letter country shows now, and an ad's never gets remembered for that brand's comments (#410).\012* With `Lock the hold speed with a pull down` on, pulling down while you hold the side of a video locks the speed again. The feed took that pull as a scroll back to the last video, or as a refresh on For You, and the hold ended before the lock could catch it. `Slide to change the hold speed` keeps its slide the same way, so a long slide no longer scrolls the feed out from under you (#422).\012* With `Let other apps play until a video starts` on, backing out of a video you opened from a chat gives your music back as fast as leaving the feed does. It used to stay paused for about two seconds (#283).\012* With `Stop video looping` on, the screen turns off on its usual timeout again once a video ends. TikTok keeps the screen lit for as long as the feed is open, so a phone left on a finished video never went dark. It stays on while anything plays (#414).\012* Saving a photo post you've already saved now says the photo post is already saved, and a photo story says the story is. The choice to open it or save it again used to call it a video, even when you'd saved it as photos (#197).\012* `Turn off haptics` also quiets Hushfeed's own buzzes now. Holding the For You, Home, Inbox or Profile tab and dragging the block button still vibrated with the switch on.\012* `Fold long comments` folds comments that TikTok already cuts with its own \"... more\". Those used to stay at TikTok's six lines. Now our more opens TikTok's cut text, and TikTok's more opens the rest.\012* When `Pause before the feed` or the daily hold comes up, TalkBack moves to its title and reads it. Coming back to TikTok from the home screen, TalkBack used to land on the Home tab and never said what was covering the feed. Once you've moved on to a button or a tab, pulling down the notification shade won't send you back to the title.\012* `Stop analytics and tracking` now says it lets through the settings TikTok downloads to check its own requests. You'll still see that download in a network capture with the switch on, since TikTok's request checks read from it (#379).\012* `Block location` also stops TikTok's own location lookup. Besides the phone's location services, TikTok asks location-v6.tiktokv.us, which works out where you are from your connection, and that request still went out with the switch on. With the switch on it's sent to your phone itself now, so it never leaves it (#379).\012* In Simplified Chinese, the Lab's Apply button said 申请, which reads as applying for something. It says 应用 now.\012* With a password on `Network proxy`, the small relay TikTok signs in through only connects to the domains TikTok uses. Another app on the phone could reach it while TikTok was open and send its own traffic through your proxy. Now it gets turned away.\012* `Hide the Hushfeed row` only takes the row out of Settings and privacy while a hold on For You or Home opens Hushfeed settings. Hiding the feed tab strip or pointing For You at your watch history used to leave no way back in. Now the row stays until a long press works again (#244).\012* `Fill the screen with the video` leaves wide and square videos whole. On a tall phone it used to zoom them in until they covered the screen, so you only saw the middle of a landscape video. Tall videos still lose the black strip under them (#394).\012* `Foldable split comment view` puts comments beside the video after you unfold with TikTok open. TikTok rebuilt the feed for the wider screen but still reported the folded width, so comments kept opening over the video until a restart. Folding back now drops the side panel too (#398).\012* A translated comment could still land in the wrong row when you scrolled fast. TikTok fades a translation in a moment after it arrives, and if the row got reused for another comment in that moment, the old comment's text was written over the new one. The fade is now called off when the row moves on (#383).\012* Patching a TikTok APK that was compiled apart from the supported one stops right away with a message naming the file to get. APKMirror added one on November 12, the 47.7.3 APK marked arm64-v8a alone, and eight patches failed on it while others hooked the wrong code (#402).\012* Two parts of TikTok reading the same new batch of feed videos at once could both run the feed filter on it and both rewrite it, and the second rewrite could crash TikTok while it was copying that batch. The filter now handles one batch at a time, so the second read finds it already done. Thanks to @Tegar30 for spotting it (#400).\012* `Auto tap` in LIVE rooms with guests keeps its taps off the guests' seats. In a grid of guests, a tap on any seat opened that person's card or the gift panel and stopped the tapping, so now it taps the open room just above or below the seats instead (#335).\012* `Foldable split comment view` works in a desktop window too, like TikTok on a Googlebook or Chromebook, in DeX or in Android's desktop mode. Those windows count as sharing the screen with other apps, so comments always came up from the bottom there, however wide the window or low the minimum width. Now the window's width decides, and dragging it across the minimum width switches the layout. Split screen still leaves comments to TikTok (#405).\012* `Fill the screen with the video` reaches the bottom on videos you open from search, a profile or a grid too. The comment bar under those videos kept a solid black strip, so filling changed nothing there. Now the video runs all the way down behind the comment bar, and the caption and buttons stay above it (#406).\012* `Blur the video behind the bar` lets go of a video once the pill isn't over it. Scroll slowly and the pill used to keep a blurred piece of the last video until the next one started playing. Now it goes back to plain glass right away (#408).\012* Hushfeed settings and the Lab scroll on under the gesture bar instead of stopping at a solid band above it, and the last row still scrolls clear of the bar (#408).\012* With `Dark LIVE panels in dark mode` on, the Blocked, Muted and Moderation lists in a LIVE's settings show their title, back arrow, help icon and Quit button in white. TikTok paints those in a fixed dark gray, so they almost vanished on the dark sheet. With `AMOLED dark theme` on, those lists are black now, like the Settings sheet they open from. They stayed gray unless you'd opened the LIVE from search (#362).\012* With `Dark LIVE panels in dark mode` on, the tip that points at the creator's message button keeps its dark text on white. It had gone white on white (#362).\012* With `Dark LIVE panels in dark mode` on, a host's pinned comment looks the way it does with the switch off, its Pinned and timer tags included. Those tags came out in other colors over the darkened room (#362).\012* With `Dark LIVE panels in dark mode` on, the Rose card that comes up the first time you tap a LIVE's quick gift reads white on its dark card. Its title and text stayed dark, so they almost vanished. The Request to join as a guest sheet goes black too, where its light text sat on a white sheet (#362).\012* With a color picked in `AMOLED dark theme` and `Dark LIVE panels in dark mode` on, the box behind the delete key in a LIVE room's emoji picker takes that color too. It was the last spot in the picker still showing TikTok's own dark gray (#329).\012* The block button and Hushfeed's other feed buttons go back to their spots after you close the picture-in-picture window and open TikTok again. They used to stay bunched up in the top corner over the feed tabs until you restarted TikTok (#413).\012* The next and previous buttons in the picture-in-picture window play the video they move to. It used to sit on its first frame with no sound, and play and pause still went to the video you left. A LIVE in the way gets skipped, since it can't play in that window (#413).\012* The Lab's `Scrolling comments on videos` preset now tells you where to look. TikTok only allows them on some wide videos, and those get an Add one-liner button under the video and a one-liner bar in full screen. The old note just said most videos stay the same (#98).\012* `Show the time beside the progress bar` counts all the way to the video's length at the end. TikTok reports where a video is a few times a second, and the last report before the end came up to a third of a second short, so a 15 second video read 0:14 / 0:15 as auto scroll moved on and looked cut off a second early (#432).\012* `Keep captions in Clear display` keeps the caption on screen after you swipe to the next video with Clear display still on. It only stayed on the first video you cleared, because TikTok clears the next video a moment before it says that video is playing (#428).\012* `Floating bottom bar` and its glass look go pale where TikTok turns its tabs black, like on Home's Community grid. The dark pill used to stay put there, so the black icons sat on a gray smear. Now the pill and the glass turn white with a thin dark edge, the lens behind your tab goes gray to match, and they go dark again as soon as you're back on the videos (#436).\012* `Stop analytics and tracking` also points TikTok's Orbu telemetry hosts, like proxy.telemetry, back at your phone, so their lookups never leave it. TikTok still looked them up on 47.7.3 with the switch on (#379).\012* The patch tests that don't read the extension run in eight groups now, one per area (feed, playback, player, sharing, messages, look, the rest of the app) plus one for the tests that read the whole source tree. An area's classpath holds only the patch classes its tests reach, and its inputs only the sources they read. Change a patch and Gradle reruns the groups whose tests reach it and the shared one, while the rest stay up to date. An edit to Hide profile tabs took 14 minutes instead of the full run's 39. Settings and navigation code reaches every group, so an edit there still reruns all of them. A full run still runs every group, and a group that finds no tests on a full run fails it.\012* The patches are built with Morphe patcher 2.4.0 now, so the next bundle needs Morphe Manager 2.6.0 or newer, or morphe-desktop 2.2.0 from a computer. Older Managers won't load it.\012\012## 0.82.0 (2026-11-12)\012\012* Hushfeed now supports TikTok 47.7.3, and only that one. 47.7.2 isn't supported anymore. Grab the 47.7.3 bundle or APK from APKMirror and patch it with the same signing key, so your login and settings carry over.\012* Hushfeed builds on Morphe patcher 2.3.0 now, so it needs Morphe Manager 2.5.0 or newer, or morphe-desktop 2.1.1 on a computer. Older Managers refuse the bundle.\012* `Jump to a date on Liked grids` puts a button in the Liked grid's top corner. Pick a year, then a month or the whole year, and your likes start there, so older ones load without scrolling through everything newer. Newest likes in the same menu goes back. It starts off and lives in Hushfeed settings > Feed screen, under the grid sort rows (#350).\012* `Show where commenters are from` also checks the country field on a commenter's account, and uses it only when it holds a two letter code (#201).\012* `Long press on Profile opens my watch history` makes holding the Profile tab show the watch history kept on your phone, so the long press on For You can keep opening Hushfeed settings. A tap on Profile works as before. It starts off, sits under `Keep my own watch history` and needs the `Feed tab navigation` patch (#172).\012* `Long-press Profile to switch accounts` brings back holding the Profile tab to pick another of your accounts, for accounts where TikTok left that hold out. A tap on Profile works as before, and while `Long-press Profile for Watch history` is on, that one gets the hold. It starts off, lives in Hushfeed settings > Feed tabs and takes a TikTok restart (#388).\012* `Discover in the bottom bar` puts Discover where Friends sits in the bottom bar, the layout TikTok gives Indonesia, and your region and feed stay as they are. It starts off, lives in Hushfeed settings > Feed tabs and takes a TikTok restart (#98).\012* `Friends in the top tabs` moves Friends up to the tabs along the top of the feed, just left of Following, and Discover takes its spot in the bottom bar, the layout TikTok gives Indonesia. Your region and feed stay as they are (#98).\012* The Feature Gate Lab can override experiments TikTok reads as a whole object, like the home tab layout. It couldn't reach those before. An override changes only the fields you give it, and it still applies when TikTok sent your account nothing for that experiment (#98).\012* The diagnostic report names the code other patch bundles added to your TikTok, or says there's none. A bundle built from the same template as Hushfeed, with the same package names, no longer counts as Hushfeed's own code. When the last crash happened inside one of them, it says which, even when TikTok's own code passed the error along. When a report runs long, `Copy quick report` now drops only the oldest events and keeps every other part whole, this one included. It also lists the last five times Android closed TikTok and why, where it used to show only the last one (#275).\012* The diagnostic export has a Font section. It shows which font TikTok's text went out in, whether an imported font loaded (and if it didn't, why), and the Samsung font style on Galaxy phones (#346).\012* Settings an update adds get a small dot after their name in Hushfeed settings, and the closed section they sit in gets one too, so you can spot what's new. A dot goes away after the visit that shows it, and a fresh install starts with none (#349).\012* `Startup message` shows a message you write each time TikTok opens, with an optional title. Turn off `Close with Back or a tap outside` and only its OK button closes it. Its `Don't show again` button hides that message until you change its title or text, or install or update TikTok again. Rotating the phone or changing TikTok's theme keeps a message you haven't closed on screen, and doesn't bring back one you have. It starts off and lives in Hushfeed settings > App (#347).\012* `Check for Hushfeed updates` tells you in TikTok when a newer Hushfeed is out. Once a day at most, when TikTok opens, it asks GitHub for the latest release, and a newer one gets a card listing the first few things it changes. Update opens Morphe Manager (or the release page if Manager isn't installed) and Dismiss hides the card for that release. The request carries your Hushfeed version and nothing else, and the switch starts off. Find it in Hushfeed settings > App, under the startup message rows (#377).\012* With a color picked in `AMOLED dark theme`'s options, Profile, Inbox and TikTok's other full pages take that color too. Before, they stayed black. The light look and the video feed don't change (#348).\012* `Block P2P video relay` also takes out the LIVE relay's two leftover libraries, about 1 MB more. The split APK bundle never had them, so nothing changes for those installs (#70).\012* `Bend the video at the edges` makes the glass pill's rim bend the blurred video behind it the way the edge of real glass does, and it gives the colors there a small lift. It sits under `Blur the video behind the bar`, starts off and needs Android 13 or newer (#231).\012* Three new switches under the ring switches, `Remove rings on the feed`, `Remove rings in comments` and `Remove rings on profiles`, pick where the story and LIVE rings come off. All three start on, so nothing changes until you turn one off (#351).\012* `Accent color` has two new options, `Like color` and `Save color`. They paint the heart on a video you liked and the bookmark on one you saved, in the feed and in their tap animations, with a preset or a color code you type. They work in light, dark and AMOLED, and with or without a new accent. Both start on TikTok's own red and yellow, which changes nothing (#369).\012* `Hide On this day` takes the On this day memory off the front of the Inbox's stories tray, and the stories after it move up into its place. It starts off and sits under `Hide stories tray` in Hushfeed settings > Inbox (#358).\012* `Hide profile pictures in comments` takes the commenter's picture off every comment and reply. The name and the comment move over to the left, so there's no empty space where the picture was. It starts off, sits under `Hide the thumbs down on comments` in Hushfeed settings > Comments and takes a TikTok restart (#352).\012* `Custom hold speed` under Playback takes any speed you type, like 1.8 or 2.3, for holding a video and for the pull-down lock under it. It takes the place of `Speed while you hold the video`, and leaving it empty keeps that row's pick (#357).\012* `Check for already-saved videos` covers `Save the original sound` too. Save a sound you already have, even from a different video that uses it, and you get Open or Save again instead of a second copy (#356).\012* `Phone model for effects` under `Report a newer phone to effects` lets you pick the phone the effects server hears about, since an effect turned down for one phone can open for another. Tap it for a list of recent Galaxy and Pixel phones, or pick `Type another model` at the bottom and enter any model yourself. Left alone it stays the Galaxy S24 Ultra (#176).\012* `Keep clear screen in the next LIVE` carries clear screen from one LIVE room to the next one you swipe to, so the chat, gifts and buttons stay hidden until you turn clear screen off. It starts off and sits in Hushfeed settings > Playback, next to `Offer clear screen in every LIVE room` (#354).\012* `LIVE feed countries` under Hushfeed settings > Region asks the LIVE feed for rooms from the countries you list, like BR, MX, taking turns page by page. TikTok doesn't say which country a room comes from, so this steers the feed instead of filtering it, and a room from somewhere else can still turn up. Nothing else in TikTok sees the change. It needs the `Region spoof` patch but none of its switches, and it starts empty (#355).\012* The diagnostic export has a Captions line. For each For You video it says whether TikTok sent caption tracks, and when it sent none, the reason TikTok gave, like not authorized or language not supported. That way an account whose captions never show can tell whether TikTok sends any at all (#217).\012* Two new switches in Hushfeed settings > Comments, `Hide the close button in comments` and `Hide the expand button in comments`, each take one button off the top of the comments, and the buttons beside it move over into its place. Back or a swipe down still closes comments. TikTok only shows the expand button to some accounts. Both start off (#371).\012* `Hide the search button on the feed` also hides the magnifying glass TikTok puts over the shrunken video while comments are open (#371).\012* `Invisible controls button` puts a small eye at the top left of the main feed. Tap it and the buttons, caption and tabs turn invisible but keep working where they are, which helps against burn-in on OLED screens. Tap the eye again and they're back. Your choice sticks across videos and restarts. The eye stays off other tabs, comments, Clear display and videos you open from a profile or search, and Pause brings everything back. `Keep the caption in sight` under it leaves the creator's name, the caption and the music line showing. Both start off and sit in Hushfeed settings > Feed screen, under `Keep faded controls in Clear display` (#374).\012* `Hide Send to new group` takes the gray Send to new group button off the share sheet when you've picked two or more people, so Send separately is the only button left. It starts off and sits under `Hide the Send to row` in Hushfeed settings > Share sheet (#375).\012* `AMOLED dark theme` has a switch now. `AMOLED dark mode` in Hushfeed settings > App starts on, and turning it off brings back TikTok's own dark grays after a restart, so you can keep the patch in and still pick plain dark mode. The color you picked in the patch's options stays for when it's on. Pause Hushfeed turns it off too (#372).\012* `Make sticker` in a video's share sheet opens TikTok's own sticker editor for that video, so you can trim it, add text and save it as an animated sticker, even on videos where TikTok doesn't show its Create sticker button. If the editor can't open, the video's cover becomes the sticker like before (#214).\012* `Automatically record LIVEs you enter` starts recording a LIVE's stream the moment you walk into the room. Swipe on to the next LIVE and that one starts recording too, while the one you left finishes saving in the background. Tap Stop and it stays stopped until you leave and come back. Screen recordings still need your tap and Android's permission. It starts off and sits under `Record LIVEs you watch` in Hushfeed settings > Playback. Thanks to Hiiva for building it (#363).\012* `Drag handle and jump buttons on grids` shows a handle at the edge of a long profile, Liked or sound grid while it moves, with Top, Back and End buttons beside it. Back returns to where you were before the last jump. It starts off and lives in Hushfeed settings > Feed screen (#378).\012* `Bottom bar icons` in Hushfeed settings > Feed tabs picks one of the icon sets TikTok is testing for the bottom bar, or leaves it to TikTok, which is how it starts. It takes a TikTok restart (#285).\012* With `Log diagnostics` on, the report keeps TikTok's answer to every LIVE like, so a like TikTok refused can be told from one that never left the phone (#380).\012* The settings screen now comes in Thai. Thanks to @MangaThatsFine (#381).\012* `Pin more chats` lets you pin more than 5 chats in the Inbox. TikTok's app stops you at 5 even though its website doesn't, and pins you make there already show up in the app. It starts off, sits under `Show inbox filters` in Hushfeed settings > Inbox and takes a TikTok restart (#385).\012* `Hide voice comments` takes voice comments out of a comment thread, replies included, the way `Hide picture comments` does for pictures and stickers. Your own v")
            .append("oice comments stay. It starts off and sits under `Hide picture comments` in Hushfeed settings > Comments.\012* `Also filter it` follows up a tap on the Not interested button. A short list offers the video's creator, its sound and up to three of its hashtags, and the one you pick goes on the feed filter's own list, so those videos stay gone even after TikTok forgets the feedback. Undo on the banner takes it back off. Cancel just closes the list, and the feedback still goes to TikTok. The sound is offered only while `Hide videos with blocked sounds` is on. It starts off and sits under `Show the Not interested button` in Hushfeed settings > Feed screen.\012* A hashtag on a word list now hides only that tag. `#cat` used to hide `#cats` and `#catholic` too, and now it leaves them alone, which is what you'd expect from a tag. Write `cat` without the # to catch every word that has it. Tags written together, like `#fyp#cat`, still count one by one. The Turkish dotted and dotless i and the Greek final sigma now match on word lists and blocked sound names however they're typed, and the keycap emoji no longer counts as a hashtag.\012* `Search Liked and Favorites grids` puts a Search button at the top of the Liked and Favorites tabs. Type a word from a caption, a creator's name or a sound and the grid shows only the loaded videos that have it, in any case, with a count of how many match. While a search is on, the grid keeps loading on its own so it looks past the first screen. Clear brings the whole grid back in its sort order. Turning the switch off (or Pause) clears the search too, so turning it back on shows the whole grid with its Search button. It starts off and sits under `Jump to a date on Liked grids` in Hushfeed settings > Feed screen.\012* `Fold long comments` cuts a long comment down to its first 4 lines with \"more\" at the end, and a tap on more opens the rest right in that row. Replies and the creator's comments fold the same way. `Fold after` sets how many lines show, from 1 to 20. It starts off and sits under `Links in comments open` in Hushfeed settings > Comments.\012* `Pause before the feed` puts a short countdown in front of For You the first time it opens after TikTok starts or comes back from the background. Continue lights up when the count ends, and Leave TikTok sends the app away instead. Messages, profiles and search open without it, and a trip to messages doesn't start the count over. It's in seconds (0 to 60), starts at 0 (off) and sits under `Don't start the first video` in Hushfeed settings > Screen time. Making it shorter waits a day when `Wait a day to loosen the budget` is on, like the budget's own numbers.\012* `Blur the video behind the bar` shows the video in the glass pill again on TikTok 47.7.3. The player now draws a smaller picture than the space it fills on screen, and the blur asked for a part of it that didn't exist, so every read failed and the pill stayed plain glass. LIVE previews in For You are found again too, since the LIVE player now builds its picture layer on its own (#259).\012* With `See-through bottom bar` or `See-through status bar` on, a video no longer shrinks for a moment and grows back right after you swipe to it. As each video starts TikTok puts the picture back to its own size, and for a moment lays the player out a little shorter, and Hushfeed now fills the picture again for the player's real size before each frame is shown (#390).\012* Saving works again behind a proxy app whose fake-IP mode answers with an IPv6 address from its own private range, like mihomo's `fdfe:dcba:9876::/64`. Hushfeed only knew the narrower fc00::/18 range, so every video and photo save stopped with \"Media URL resolves to a non-public address\". Any private IPv6 range a fake-IP proxy hands out counts now, and when a save is still turned down for a local address, the message names the range instead of saying nothing (#387).\012* A comment row could show the translated text of the comment it held before. TikTok reuses rows as you scroll, and a row it reused for a picture or sticker comment kept listening for the old comment's translation, so a translation landing for that comment afterwards (from `Auto translate comments`, say) showed up in the wrong row until you scrolled. A row now stops listening for its old comment as soon as it gets a new one. With `Auto translate comments` on, a row could also keep the other video's comment when you opened one video's comments right after another's, because the translation request went out while TikTok was still filling the row in. It now waits until the row is done (#383).\012* With `Hide unpersonalized For You videos` on, a For You batch that's nothing but fill-in now keeps just its first video instead of all of them, so far fewer unpicked videos slip through while the feed still has somewhere to go. Thanks to @yokkkoso (#391).\012* A mouse wheel or touchpad scroll over the daily hold, the tap to start stop, the App lock screen, the Start page cover or the profile grid's sort hold no longer scrolls what's behind it. A hold too tall for the screen scrolls itself instead.\012* On the App lock screen TalkBack goes straight to Unlock and reads \"TikTok is locked\" along with it. It used to stop on the title by itself first.\012* With App lock on and `Open TikTok on` set to Inbox, Profile or another tab, TalkBack and Tab reach Unlock right away while TikTok opens. The start screen used to hide the lock screen from them for up to 8 seconds.\012* During the daily hold, pressing the right arrow key on the last tab no longer slides TikTok over to a creator's profile, and TalkBack's scroll actions can't page it there either. Arrow keys still move between the tabs and the hold's buttons.\012* `Latest first on Following` loads further ahead. TikTok sends only a few posts per read on Following and asked for more just three posts before the end, so a newer post often showed up after you'd already scrolled past older ones. With the switch on, the next read starts while about a dozen posts are still waiting below you, so more of them are sorted before you get there. With it off, Following loads the way TikTok does (#226).\012* While App lock is up, a dialog, sheet or popup TikTok opens no longer shows on top of the lock screen or takes a tap. One that was already open when TikTok locked goes behind it too, and after you unlock they're back as they were.\012* `Remove LIVE extras` leaves the files LIVE invitations, co-hosting, joining as a guest and battle scores run on alone now. Picking every patch used to empty the guest call library, so friends' invitations never showed up and joining a LIVE failed. The patch is down to the LIVE games script and animated gift effects, so it saves very little space now (#382, #107, #132).\012* `Icon picture` in `Custom launcher icon` takes the folder Morphe Manager's picker hands back. It uses the only PNG in that folder, or the one named `icon.png` when there are several, and otherwise stops and names the PNGs it found. The hidden `._` copies a Mac leaves next to each picture on a memory card don't count, and a folder that can't be read says so instead of claiming it holds no PNG. Before, picking a folder stopped patching with \"there's no file\" until you typed the file name in by hand (Discussion #288).\012* With `Check for already-saved videos` on, saving something you already have no longer flashes \"Saving\" right before Open or Save again comes up. That note now waits until the check finds it's new, for sounds, original photos and photo posts saved as a video (#356).\012* A LIVE quality you pick stays picked after TikTok restarts as soon as `Offer LIVE quality in more rooms` is on. `Keep the LIVE quality after TikTok restarts` used to start off as well, so the next launch opened rooms at Auto again. It starts on now, and you can still turn it off (#353).\012* With `Hide CAPTCHA popups` off, which is how it starts, a puzzle that shows while you're just browsing (in a LIVE room, say) now gets a short note naming that switch. It shows once a session, and never for a puzzle the switch would show anyway, like a sign-in check (#87).\012* Hiding Report from the share sheet doesn't take `Block this creator` with it anymore. Block sits where Report would have been, in the share sheet and in the long-press menu (#367).\012* With `Open TikTok on` set to Profile, Inbox, Friends or Discover, For You doesn't flash up for a second before that tab anymore. TikTok always builds Home first, so the start screen now stays up until your tab is showing (#360).\012* With `Open TikTok on` set to Profile, Inbox, Friends or Discover, the phone's Back no longer drops you on For You. Back from another tab takes you to the one TikTok opens on, and Back there closes TikTok the way it closes any other app. When `Search instead of Home` or the feed lock has TikTok open on Inbox or Profile instead, Back follows that tab. Picking For You or Following keeps TikTok's own Back (#360).\012* With `Let other apps play until a video starts` on, your music comes back about a quarter second after you leave a paused video for the inbox, a chat or a profile. It used to stay quiet for a second or two first (#283).\012* A bio handle with a period and a date stuck to it, like @john.doe11/30/24, stays plain text now. In 0.81.0 it linked only the part before the period, which opened a different account (#247).\012* With `Long-press Profile for Watch history` on, holding Profile opens Watch history again after you remove your second account. Before, the hold did nothing until TikTok rebuilt its tab bar (#341).\012* Hushfeed adds less lag when a video opens from Search or Explore. The part that hides buttons on videos rebuilt its whole lookup list on every screen layout while the page opened, and now builds it once. With `Playback quality` set, each video's addresses get checked once too, instead of again in every place the player asks (#344).\012* LIVE Auto tap taps the host's side of the stream now. In a battle or a room with guests it used to tap near the middle, hit the other creator's half and open their profile card, which stopped it after a second. If a tap still opens a card, the next start in that room skips that spot (#335).\012* With `LIVE recording source` set to Screen, a recording keeps going after you allow it. Android's permission screen made TikTok think you were leaving the room, so TikTok shrank the LIVE into its own picture-in-picture window and the recording stopped a few seconds in.\012* On some phones the screen blinked each time a video slid under the bar with `See-through bottom bar` on. The new `Stop the blink under the bar` switch under it has TikTok draw the video inside its own window instead of on a separate layer, which those phones were dropping for a frame. It starts off and takes a TikTok restart (#232).\012* `See-through bottom bar` works on the Following tab too. TikTok keeps a strip the height of the bar at the bottom of that feed and paints it black, so the video there still stopped above the tabs. That strip goes clear with the switch now (#232).\012* With `See-through bottom bar` on, the still picture TikTok shows while a video starts lines up with the video when TikTok has moved the video up a little. It used to sit higher than the video, with a dark strip under it (#232).\012* An imported font and `Use system font` now reach TikTok's own screens, like its Settings pages, on installs patched from the split APK bundle. TikTok's fonts aren't in the bundle, so TikTok had nothing to swap and fell back to the phone's default font. Bold text stays bold (#346).\012* `Hide TikTok Shop` also hides the \"Find <product>\" button with the shopping bag that sits above the search bar on some videos. 0.81.0 only caught a different Find bar, and the diagnostic export now counts this button on its own line (#271).\012* `Remove story rings` and `Remove the LIVE ring` take the rings off on the feed, in comments and on profiles again. TikTok 47.7.2 hands each picture its story status directly and asks a different place whether someone's live, so the old hooks missed most of them. The stories trays at the top of the Inbox, Following and Friends keep their rings, because TikTok takes anyone without one out of the tray (#351).\012* `AMOLED dark theme` reaches the popup that says \"You'll see fewer posts like this\" after Not interested, the comments' sort menu and TikTok's other toasts and small popup menus. They stayed gray before (#368).\012* With `AMOLED dark theme` on, the X that closes the comments no longer sits on a gray circle. The circle takes the AMOLED color now, along with other buttons and rows on TikTok's sheets drawn in that same gray. Turning off `AMOLED dark mode` brings the gray back (#371).\012* With `Dark LIVE panels in dark mode` on, the names in a LIVE's moderator settings and its muted and blocked lists read white on the dark sheet. They came out dark gray before. The \"Support this LIVE\" bubble over the gift button keeps its dark text on white too, where it had turned white on white (#362).\012* `Remove creation tools` keeps the camera's face model and the effect editor library now, so face effects, Retouch and All effects work with it in. It still takes out the two big effects engine libraries TikTok doesn't load for any of that, about 45 MB, on the APK and on the bundle alike (#285).\012* The Suggested accounts heading in the Inbox lines its title and info icon up with `Clear all` again. Hushfeed's taller Clear all button had pushed them up above it (#358).\012* With `Compact comment header` on, the translate and close buttons no longer sit on top of the first comment. TikTok 47.7.2 moved them out of the header into their own row, so they stayed behind when the header went away. They're hidden along with the rest of the header now (#358).\012* Profiles with their own stickers show the Stickers tab again on TikTok 47.7.3, and tapping it opens their sticker sets and video stickers instead of a \"Something went wrong\" page (#214).\012* With `Dark LIVE panels in dark mode` on, Video quality under a LIVE's Share menu is dark all the way through. Its sheet went dark before, but the list of qualities sat on a white card with dark text, and its close X was nearly black on black (#168).\012* The install steps now say to patch TikTok with Hushfeed's patches alone, since another source picked beside it can add to the memory patching needs. They also say what fit in tests with the 1 GB a 32-bit Manager can give the patcher. Simple mode's patches did, and so did every patch at once except with `AMOLED dark theme` and `Region spoof` both on, so turn on only one of them there (#339, #252).\012* Patching with Simple mode's patches needs less memory. `Allow screenshots and Circle to Search` no longer rewrites the spots in TikTok that only keep the screen on or go full screen, which is about half the ones it touched. On 47.7.3 that's 1324 classes rebuilt instead of 1460, and patching now finishes with 832 MB where it used to need 896 MB (#339).\012* Patching with Simple mode's patches needs less memory again. `Turn off haptics` no longer rewrites the 443 spots where TikTok gives a view a long-press action. It quiets the long-press buzz from TikTok's screens instead, while your finger is down, and text fields keep their selection buzz. On 47.7.3 that's 1057 classes rebuilt instead of 1324, and patching finishes with 768 MB (#339).\012* With a color picked in `AMOLED dark theme`, a LIVE room's comment bar, its emoji picker and the boxes behind the picker's send and delete buttons take that color under `Dark LIVE panels in dark mode`. They used to stay TikTok's own dark gray, so a tinted theme showed two shades there. With the default black they look the same as before (#329).\012* The build no longer pulls in a Guava or Netty release with known advisories against it. Guava moves to 33.8.0, past CVE-2026-118042, and the Netty that Android's test tools bring along moves to 4.1.139, past a critical netty-handler advisory. None of it reaches the app on your phone.\012* The README's install steps name the TikTok version a release was built for once that release is out. 0.80.0 and 0.81.0 went out with the steps still pointing at the TikTok before it.\012* `Disable telemetry` also stops TikTok's Orbu log upload and its whoami lookups, which were still going out on 47.7.3 (#379).\012* `Hide surveys` takes the interest buttons off a video by their own view as well, for when TikTok builds them some other way. The diagnostic report now names each kind of feed component a video was given (#293).\012* Blocking a LIVE host with `Block this creator` and swiping to the next room before the block went through no longer closes the room you moved to.\012* TalkBack reads the sort button on a profile, Liked or sound grid as a button and says the order it's on, like \"Sort this grid: Original order\". It only said \"Sort this grid\" before. The count that shows while a sorted grid loads reads as \"30 videos\" now, where it was a bare number.\012* On a phone set to Arabic or another right-to-left language, the button rows in What's new, the sticker sheet and the Feature Gate Lab run right to left now. The gaps inside the search box, a recent search, the status card and the notices are mirrored to match. In the Lab, a gate's title no longer runs into its value and `Apply overrides` keeps some space from its switch, whichever way the screen reads.\012* On a right-to-left phone, a setting's description now sits under its name on the icon's side, and a section's heading starts on that side too. Hushfeed's text is English, so those lines used to start at the far left, across the row from the name.\012* `Hide the LIVE button` now shows the restart button when you flip it, like the search and side menu switches. Turned off, the LIVE button stayed missing with nothing telling you it needed a restart.\012* If you left a video cleared with `Keep Clear display across videos` on, the first video after you reopen TikTok clears too, instead of keeping its buttons. Its tabs and buttons also stay hidden while TikTok gets ready to clear it, so they don't flash up first.\012* With `Hide CAPTCHA popups` on, tapping hearts in a LIVE no longer hides TikTok's check. It shows, the same as it does for a save or a gift, because a hidden check left the hearts on screen while TikTok counted none of them. When TikTok turns your taps down, Hushfeed says so once, the way it does for a video like (#380).\012* The sort button and the jump buttons on profile, Liked and sound grids sit on a darker backdrop, so their words read over a white or busy thumbnail (#378).\012* The hold speed bubble follows your phone's font size now, in both the pill and the round dial. With large text on, the speed used to stay small while everything else in Hushfeed grew. The whole bubble grows with it, so the padlock and the dots keep their room.\012* With `Open TikTok on` set to Inbox, Profile or another tab, TalkBack can't land on the For You feed hidden under the start screen while TikTok opens.\012* Restoring a settings backup, resetting settings or undoing either one now updates the feed's text size and color, the commenter names, a searched Liked or Favorites grid, the buttons on the video, feed mute, the comment search box and kept captions right away, the same as flipping those switches by hand. A grid you'd searched stayed narrowed after a restore turned `Search Liked and Favorites grids` off. If one of those can't redraw, the rest still do.\012* A switch your patch options turned on now works from the first launch, including the privacy and speed switches TikTok reads before Hushfeed's settings load. Those early reads treated them as off until you'd flipped them yourself.\012* `Included diagnostics` shows the choice a restored backup brought back. A saved choice it doesn't know now includes everything, where it used to export an empty log.\012* When `Turn back on` can't save, it says \"Couldn't save the change. Try again.\" instead of acting like Hushfeed came back on.\012* Shared diagnostics leave out email addresses, phone numbers, account names and your proxy's address. Phone numbers written with spaces, dashes or brackets go too, and so does a nickname of several words or the name in front of your proxy's or router's address. A name with a smiley, an apostrophe or a comma in it is left out whole, and so is one written after a folder path. A time zone like +1000 next to a log's timestamp stays, since it isn't a phone number. A value that starts on the next line of a logged message goes too, along with any password or token written inside it, and a stack trace under an empty field stays readable. Details logged after a video's id, like its place in the feed, stay readable too. Text inside logged JSON, even JSON quoted inside other JSON, is now read like any other text, so a name or number tucked in there goes the same way. Version numbers like 4.12.0.1 and stack trace lines from Scala code stay readable.\012* Opening a video from a sorted or searched Liked grid, or from your sorted private videos, now swipes in the grid's order, and a search plays its matches first. Those two grids have a tap handler of their own, so their video page kept TikTok's order while your posts followed the sort (#180).\012* On TikTok 47.7.3 the Favorites tab gets its sort button, position rail and Search button. TikTok tucks that grid inside an extra container there, so none of them showed up, and they now sit just under the Posts and Collections row (#180).\012* A background job that fails, like the media cache's start-up cleanup, now shows up in the diagnostics log. Before, nothing recorded it.\012* On the light theme, the shine that runs across the Hushfeed settings title no longer washes the letters out. It's softer there now, so the title stays readable while it passes.\012* TalkBack doesn't stop on the screen that holds the feed as a whole anymore. It used to read everything on it a second time and offer to activate it, which did nothing. The title, the countdown and both buttons are still read one by one.\012* Tab on a keyboard or d-pad can't wander into the feed behind the daily hold anymore. It used to move from the hold into the video and the like and comment buttons underneath. Now it goes between the hold's buttons and the tabs along the bottom, which TalkBack can reach again too.\012* With the feed lock on, coming back to TikTok no longer puts the \"Tap to start the feed\" layer on top of the lock screen. It took the first tap there, which could start a video behind the lock.\012* With App lock up, Tab goes straight to Unlock. It used to stop on the black screen first, and TalkBack offered to press that screen, which did nothing. Anything TikTok opens while it's locked stays behind the lock screen too.\012")
            .toString();

    /** The translated notes for a settings table tag (lower case, as L10n reads it), or null. */
    public static String translated(String tag) {
        if (tag == null) return null;
        switch (tag) {
            default: return null;
        }
    }
